    process:["A clinician reviews symptoms and screens for infection, prolapse, genitourinary syndrome of menopause and type of urinary leakage.","The device, regulatory status, evidence, alternatives and limitations are discussed. An in-person pelvic assessment may be required.","If appropriate and consented, focused ultrasound is delivered according to device protocol. Follow-up evaluates symptoms—not only appearance."],
    risks:"Potential risks include pain, burns or thermal injury, bleeding, infection, altered sensation, scarring, pain with intercourse and failure to improve. Evidence and FDA status vary by device and claimed indication. Identity Aesthetics does not promise “mind-boggling” tightening or cure of urinary incontinence.",
